/**
 * The weak `keep` law's baseline (ADR 0033 decision 7; PS4.3 design §7 K1): per file, SHA-256 of
 * `keepWeakLawPayload` (`./keep-weak-law.ts`: every storey's SVG, `describe()` with and without
 * `--facts depends`, `lint()`, `compile().diagnostics`, `validate --json`, `impact --json`) and the
 * resolution's evaluation-step count.
 *
 * GENERATED by `npx tsx test/keep-weak-law-gen.ts`, with the test's own body. First taken on the
 * tree BEFORE the `keep` statement existed and committed on its own, so the next commit's diff proved
 * the law. Never hand-edited. A moved row is a finding to explain (`docs/testing.md` §3): when a later
 * PR legitimately moves a hashed output (never keep code), the table is re-taken by the generator, the
 * reason recorded below and the moved files listed in that commit's message.
 *
 * Taken: re-taken on feat/lint-stairs-ps211e (PR #280, over main@52e7c71f): the PS2.11e stair rules moved lint()/validate() of keep-free files (listed in the commit). Earlier: main@c2f4176b, after PR #271 added describe().totals.gross_internal_area_m2 (and gross_internal_area_all_levels_m2) to every resolving plan; 269 files re-taken on this tree before any keep code (first taken on main@5aab29e5, re-taken on main@0c5e7a09)
 */

